/**
 * Codex app-server protocol types, and the narrow envelope shapes we read off
 * the wire.
 *
 * The types are **referenced in place** from `resources/codex-protocol/` rather
 * than copied into `src/`. That directory is generated by
 * `codex app-server generate-ts` and is the source of truth (HANDOFF fact 5);
 * copying it here would mean 642 files to re-sync by hand every time Codex
 * moves. Every import below is `import type`, so nothing survives compilation
 * and the `resources/` tree never enters the bundle or the test runtime.
 * `tsconfig.json` excludes `resources/` from its include globs, but exclude
 * only filters those globs -- files pulled in by an import are still part of
 * the program, which is why this typechecks.
 *
 * This module re-exports only what the adapter actually uses, so the rest of
 * the adapter has one place to look and one place to fix if Codex renames
 * something.
 */

